<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shanxi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shanxi is a province of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and iron. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> profile notes that coal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-smelting">iron production</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> and Shanxi reached a scale not surpassed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> until the eighteenth century. The region was a centre of Song proto-industrial growth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shanxi.jpg" alt="Shanxi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Underbar dk · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yanmenguan3.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
